From 524ec614d2b1bcb44486056f1edc88205918c99e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 03:14:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02491/11362] [outer-loop] induction arm result: stronger
 proposer (Qwen-35B) 0/6, identical no-op to gemma-12B

Valid Qwen-35B test (isolated port 8920) = 0/6 on the gap-1 games, byte-identical action counts to
gemma-12B (ar25 7763, cn04 7843, ka59 7728, sc25 7677, sk48 7859, wa30 7818) => the E3 induce->verify->
plan produced a NO-OP plan in both -> model SIZE is not the lever; the induction PIPELINE is. Both cheap
arms now ruled out with proof (value-net LOGO ~chance; stronger proposer identical no-op). Next: INSTRUMENT
the E3 pipeline (induced-engine accuracy + does plan_in_model return a plan) to find the failing STAGE.
(arc_leaderboard_eval.py port-8920 fix landed via conductor checkpoint 3186a06a4.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
